## Run it locally

```bash
wp --require=deploy/deploy.php restore
```

This builds the site and copies it into this folder. It needs Node.js (`npx`), `rsync` and `git`.
It never touches `wp-config.php`, the database, `deploy/` or `.git`.

To run the blueprint alone in WordPress Playground:

```bash
wp --require=deploy/deploy.php vendor fetch
npx @wp-playground/cli@latest server --blueprint=./blueprint.json --blueprint-may-read-adjacent-files
```

A rebuild installs the zip wordpress.org serves today. If an author edited a released version
(a readme, line endings), a file can differ in a harmless way. The published checksums accept both.

